{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqquqci425x","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"agentic LLM grader is additive on top of the kept single shot floor never regress below it","summary":"BINDING design constraint for the LLM search-loop integration (task #4, feature code-graph-llm-retrieval): the proven single-shot best-effort top-k retrieval (the 0.705 winner; plus Part 1 structural-edge neighbors) is the KEPT WINNING PATH and the GUARANTEED FLOOR of the agentic search output. The LLM grader sits ON TOP as a purely ADDITIVE layer — it may add rounds, reformulate the query from intent, re-rank/keep by intent, and aggregate — but the returned context must always be superset-or-equal to the single-shot floor for a retrieval intent and must NEVER abstain below it. Rationale: single-shot wins precisely BECAUSE it never abstains (always returns top-k); replacing it with the LLM controller risks reintroducing the abstention regression that scored agentic 0.346 (abstaining on 7/13). So the grader's 'abstain' means 'nothing to ADD beyond the floor', not 'return nothing'. The heuristic ranker stays as the cheap top-N prefilter feeding BOTH the floor and the LLM. Enforced at integration (task #4), not in the grader module (task #3) which only grades candidates.","category":"project","tags":[],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-23T16:21:29.164Z","vec":[-0.0011039086384698749,-0.014353333041071892,-0.06591715663671494,-0.04721670597791672,0.04694423824548721,0.05009961873292923,-0.00975900050252676,0.056828320026397705,-0.0029552807100117207,0.018445849418640137,0.01869315840303898,-0.004665938671678305,0.10556882619857788,-0.00811082310974598,-0.01662413403391838,0.040956560522317886,0.15941011905670166,0.010938961990177631,-0.05221179127693176,-0.031546950340270996,0.05931001901626587,-0.023912372067570686,0.08099125325679779,-0.004579517059028149,-0.006856862455606461,-0.0304122157394886,-0.07927843183279037,0.024509329348802567,0.09438168257474899,-0.08230161666870117,0.